#title[Next discriminating design — conditional]
#sub[Rank 1: same-48 / all-six exact density]
Design a separately frozen independent census of every nonzero state per current fixed curve/function. Preserve errors, erasures, caps, list budget, conversion and both public checks. Establish any Hamming-condition/recovery equivalence explicitly. Compare exact per-cell q against the same-domain average min(M(s),r−1)/(r−1).

A positive q plus a proved fresh uniform-blinding map can qualify recovery on that fixed function; it does not establish a family or complexity result. Pay all census/orbit/log work as diagnostic work. No table or label advice enters the candidate and no result guides target/function selection.

Prior EXP-ECDLP-8dc19d already has small exact censuses at r=17,29,61,127, including the r17 q=8/16 working example. Its implementation refuses larger r. The proposed extension concerns these current 48 ordinary 10/13/16-bit curves, all six cells, current mask and M(s). Current exact densities are not computed here.

Controls: true-half positive, negated-half refusal under stated length/cap premises, actual prior anchored-odd q0 fixtures, erasure/cap/list boundaries and wrong scalar/conversion. Blind independent predictions precede source/result access. Reconcile every retained trace/recovery. Mismatch preserves a smallest witness; incomplete enumeration/custody remains inconclusive.

